```

---

# Symptoms of Corrupted System Files

Common signs include:

- Random crashes
- Missing Windows features
- Error messages
- Windows tools not opening
- Unusual behavior
- System instability

---

# How to Run SFC

## Step 1

Open:

```text
Command Prompt (Administrator)
```

## Step 2

Run:

```text
sfc /scannow
```

## Step 3

Wait for the scan to complete.

The process may take several minutes.

---

# Possible SFC Results

## No Problems Found

```text
Windows Resource Protection did not find any integrity violations.
```

Meaning:

```text
System Files Healthy
```

---

## Problems Found and Repaired

```text
Windows Resource Protection found corrupt files and successfully repaired them.
```

Meaning:

```text
Corruption Found
↓
Successfully Fixed
```

---

## Problems Found but Not Repaired

```text
Windows Resource Protection found corrupt files but was unable to fix some of them.
```

Meaning:

```text
Further Troubleshooting Required
```

---

# Why SFC Is Useful

Instead of reinstalling Windows immediately:

```text
Problem Appears
↓
Run SFC
↓
Repair Corrupted Files
↓
Test Again
```

This often saves time and effort.

---

# Professor's Gold Rule #13

> When Windows acts strangely, check system files before reinstalling Windows.

